    "name": "max-gap-leave-stops-the-clock-and-an-off-roster-rotation-does-not",
    "why": "Owner decision I's two halves, on one person each, in one world — because they are one line apart in an implementation and a month of different behaviour on a rota. p-ali is off the roster from the 6th to the 17th and their nineteen-day gap is measured in full: MR-04's per-person include/exclude override has no column anywhere in this repository, and inferring one from a gap in unitSpans would be exactly what RotaAccessTest exists to refuse. p-noor is on LEAVE for the same twelve days and their identical nineteen-day gap measures seven, because a person cannot be scheduled on their own leave. The case carries the kinds filter too: p-ali's backup duty on the 10th would split the gap into nine and ten and clear it entirely if the rule counted every kind rather than calls.",
